because as I wrote here https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/26919#issuecomment-2692186469
The assertion only happens after a full round of the reader_idx is happening,
and the state of the QP has also a full cycle:
OBTAINED (but directly after the wait loop) -> RETIRED -> ALLOCATED -> OBTAINED (but still in the wait loop)
So the assertion must check if the QP is now in RETIRED then it is a failure,
if it is ALLOCATED or OBTAINED we assume that the wait loop is still running.

